%N A218962 Total number of maximal abelian subgroups of the alternating group, counting conjugates as distinct.
%H A218962 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A218962/b218962.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..40</a>
%H A218962 Liam Naughton and Goetz Pfeiffer, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1211.1911">Integer sequences realized by the subgroup pattern of the symmetric group</a>, arXiv:1211.1911 [math.GR], 2012-2013 and <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL16/Naughton/naughton2.html">J. Int. Seq. 16 (2013) #13.5.8</a>
%H A218962 Liam Naughton, <a href="https://maths.nuigalway.ie/~liam/CountingSubgroups.g">CountingSubgroups.g</a>
%H A218962 Liam Naughton and Goetz Pfeiffer, <a href="https://gap-packages.github.io/tomlib/">Tomlib, The GAP table of marks library</a>
%F A218962 From _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 24 2026: (Start)
%F A218962 Let r_m^+ (resp. r_m^-) be the number of regular Abelian subgroups of S_m that are contained (resp. not contained) in A_m.
%F A218962 E(x) = Sum_{m>=2} r_m^+*x^m/m!, O(x) = Sum_{m>=2} r_m^-*x^m/m!.
%F A218962 E.g.f.: Sum_{n>=0} a(n)*x^n/n! = exp(E(x))*((1+x)*(exp(O(x))-O(x)-x^4/8)+x^2/2).
%F A218962 If m = 2^a*q, where a >= 1 and q is odd, then
%F A218962 r_m^- = (m-1)!*A058162(q)/(2^(a-1)*(q-1)!),
%F A218962 and r_m^+ = A058162(m)-r_m^-.
%F A218962 If m is odd, r_m^- = 0 and r_m^+ = A058162(m).(End)
%Y A218962 Cf. A218957 (maximal Abelian subgroups of the symmetric group), A058162 (number of labeled Abelian groups with a fixed identity).
%K A218962 nonn,changed
%O A218962 0,5
%A A218962 _Liam Naughton_, Nov 23 2012
%E A218962 a(3)-a(13) corrected by _Liam Naughton_, Jul 17 2018
%E A218962 a(14) and beyond from _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 24 2026
